        "original_id": "0ea3aaf3-10ab-572e-9254-a70c8b6798b7",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Works: Splendor in the Grass, Let's Scare Jessica to Death\n- People: Elia Kazan, William Inge, David Amram, Zohra Lampert, Natalie Wood, Warren Beatty\n- Topics: film careers, screenplay, direction, acting\n\nFacts:\n- Elia Kazan was born as Elias Kazantzoglou on September 7, 1909, and he became a Greek-American director, producer, writer, and actor whom The New York Times described as one of the most honored and influential directors in Broadway and Hollywood history.\n- Zohra Lampert was born on May 13, 1937, and she became an American actress with roles in film, television, and stage.\n- Splendor in the Grass is a 1961 Technicolor drama film about a teenage girl dealing with sexual repression, love, and heartbreak.\n- Splendor in the Grass was written by William Inge, who briefly appeared in the film as a Protestant clergyman and won an Oscar for the screenplay.\n- Splendor in the Grass was directed by Elia Kazan and features a score by jazz composer David Amram.\n- Zohra Lampert starred alongside Natalie Wood and Warren Beatty in the 1961 film Splendor in the Grass.\n- Zohra Lampert played the title character in the 1971 cult horror film Let's Scare Jessica to Death.\n- Elia Kazan died on September 28, 2003.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
